IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art02-making`

-- je21-art11-annulment: Article 11 (States power to annul Jersey subordinate legislation not made by the States) of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021).
--
-- A "sitting" is not defined in the Law, so a sitting is a count the caller gives: the number of sittings of the States held after the date on which the instrument was laid,
-- up to and including the sitting at which the States resolved that it be annulled.
-- The date of laying itself is not needed for the answer, because the count is measured from it.
-- This module adds no dates and counts no days.
--
-- Article 11(4) says that for subordinate legislation made before the commencement of Part 2 "the reference in paragraph (1) to 3 sittings after it is made is construed as meaning 3 sittings after the commencement of this Part".
-- Paragraph (1) has no reference to "3 sittings after it is made": it says "3 sittings after the date on which it is laid" (src:108).
-- That is the fork L7: the brief's reading and the literal text of (4) run the 3 sittings from the commencement of Part 2, which is 28 September 2021 (endnotes); the other reading takes (4) to have nothing to apply to.
-- The brief's first reading of Article 11(4) glossed this difference away; NOTES.md section 10 reports it.
--
-- "made before the commencement of this Part" on 28 September 2021 itself turns on the time of day at which Part 2 came into force, which is fork L3 (see je21-art03-commencement.l4).

§ `Article 11 -- States power to annul Jersey subordinate legislation not made by the States`

§§ `11(3) The instruments Article 11 applies to`

-- Answers: does Article 11 apply to this instrument?
-- It applies to Jersey subordinate legislation that is not made by the States, other than legislation providing purely for the commencement of any legislation.
-- The reading of "made by the States" is fork L5 (je21-art02-making).
-- Fork L12: "This Article applies to any Jersey subordinate legislation that is not made by the States other than ..." names what the Article covers.
-- On the reading taken, an instrument outside the clause (a Law or UK extended legislation, which are not Jersey subordinate legislation, or an instrument made by the States) is not within Article 11 and the answer is FALSE;
-- on the other the Law does not say whether Article 11 reaches it, and the model refuses.
-- Legislation providing purely for commencement is excluded by the words "other than", so it is FALSE on both readings.
-- src:112 | (3) This Article applies to any Jersey subordinate legislation that is not made by the States other than legislation providing purely for the commencement of any legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 11(3) (src:112)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of legislation`
      `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reading of legislation made by the States` IS A `Reading L5 of legislation made by the States`
      `the reading of an applicability clause` IS A `Reading L12 of an applicability clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11(3): Article 11 applies to the instrument` form `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation` `the reading of legislation made by the States` `the reading of an applicability clause` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `a Law` THEN `Article 11(3): what lies outside the clause` `the reading of an applicability clause`
    WHEN `UK extended legislation` THEN `Article 11(3): what lies outside the clause` `the reading of an applicability clause`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `Article 2: the legislation was made by the States` form `the reading of legislation made by the States`
        THEN `Article 11(3): what lies outside the clause` `the reading of an applicability clause`
        ELSE NOT `it provides purely for the commencement of any legislation`

-- Answers: what does the reading of an applicability clause make of an instrument outside Article 11(3)?
GIVEN `the reading of an applicability clause` IS A `Reading L12 of an applicability clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11(3): what lies outside the clause` `the reading of an applicability clause` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading of an applicability clause`
    WHEN `an applicability clause is exhaustive, so what lies outside it is not within the Article` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an applicability clause only names what it includes, so the Law does not say whether the Article reaches what lies outside it`
        THEN REFUSE "Article 11(3) says Article 11 applies to Jersey subordinate legislation that is not made by the States, other than legislation providing purely for the commencement of any legislation, and the Law does not say whether Article 11 applies to any other instrument"

§§ `11(1) The duty to lay`

-- Answers: must this instrument be laid before the States as soon as practicable after it is made?
-- It must if Article 11 applies.
-- Whether it was laid "as soon as practicable" is a judgement the caller makes, and is the second input.
-- src:108 | (1) Subordinate legislation to which this Article applies must be laid before the States as soon as practicable after it is made and if the States no later than 3 sittings after the date on which it is laid, resolve that it be annulled, it ceases to have effect.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 11(1) (src:108)
GIVEN `Article 11 applies to the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was laid as soon as practicable after it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11(1): the duty to lay the instrument before the States has been met` `Article 11 applies to the instrument` `it was laid as soon as practicable after it was made` MEANS
    IF `Article 11 applies to the instrument`
    THEN `it was laid as soon as practicable after it was made`
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 11 does not apply to the instrument, so it does not say that the instrument must be laid"

§§ `11(1), 11(2)(a) and 11(4) Ceasing to have effect`

-- Answers: has the instrument ceased to have effect under Article 11?
-- It has if Article 11 applies, the empowering Law has no contrary provision displacing paragraph (1), and the States resolved that it be annulled no later than 3 sittings after the date on which it was laid.
-- For an instrument made before the commencement of Part 2 the 3 sittings run from the commencement of Part 2 on the reading taken (L7).
-- FALSE means the States did not annul it in time, or did not resolve to.
-- Where Article 11 does not apply to the instrument, or a contrary provision in the empowering Law displaces paragraph (1), the Law says nothing of what ends the instrument, and the model refuses.
-- src:108 | (1) Subordinate legislation to which this Article applies must be laid before the States as soon as practicable after it is made and if the States no later than 3 sittings after the date on which it is laid, resolve that it be annulled, it ceases to have effect.
-- src:110 | (a) paragraph (1) may be displaced by any contrary provision in the Law empowering the subordinate legislation; and
-- src:113 | (4) In the case of Jersey subordinate legislation that was made before the commencement of this Part, the reference in paragraph (1) to 3 sittings after it is made is construed as meaning 3 sittings after the commencement of this Part.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 11(1), (2)(a) and (4) (src:108, src:110, src:113)
GIVEN `Article 11 applies to the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the instrument was made` IS A DATE
      `the States resolved that it be annulled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sittings after the date on which it was laid, up to the sitting of the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the sittings after the commencement of Part 2, up to the sitting of the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `a contrary provision in the empowering Law displaces paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reading of Article 11(4)` IS A `Reading L7 of Article 11(4)`
      `the reading of the time at which the Law came into force` IS A `Reading L3 of the time at which the Law came into force`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11: the instrument has ceased to have effect` `Article 11 applies to the instrument` `the day on which the instrument was made` `the States resolved that it be annulled` `the sittings after the date on which it was laid, up to the sitting of the resolution` `the sittings after the commencement of Part 2, up to the sitting of the resolution` `a contrary provision in the empowering Law displaces paragraph (1)` `the reading of Article 11(4)` `the reading of the time at which the Law came into force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Article 11 applies to the instrument`
            THEN REFUSE "Article 11 does not apply to the instrument, so it does not say that a resolution of the States ends it"
        IF `a contrary provision in the empowering Law displaces paragraph (1)`
            THEN REFUSE "Article 11(2)(a) lets a contrary provision in the Law empowering the instrument displace paragraph (1), and the Law does not say what ends the instrument when one does"
        IF NOT `the States resolved that it be annulled` THEN FALSE
        IF `the day on which the instrument was made` LESS THAN YMD 2021 9 28
            THEN CONSIDER `the reading of Article 11(4)`
                 WHEN `the 3 sittings run from the commencement of Part 2, which is what paragraph (4) says`
                     THEN `the sittings after the commencement of Part 2, up to the sitting of the resolution` AT MOST 3
                 WHEN `paragraph (4) has no reference to apply to, so the 3 sittings run from the date of laying, as paragraph (1) says`
                     THEN `the sittings after the date on which it was laid, up to the sitting of the resolution` AT MOST 3
        IF `the day on which the instrument was made` GREATER THAN YMD 2021 9 28
            THEN `the sittings after the date on which it was laid, up to the sitting of the resolution` AT MOST 3
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the reading of the time at which the Law came into force`
            WHEN `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)`
                THEN `the sittings after the date on which it was laid, up to the sitting of the resolution` AT MOST 3
            WHEN `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`
                THEN REFUSE "the sources do not say at what time of day on 28 September 2021 Part 2 of the Law came into force, so whether an instrument made that day was made before it cannot be answered"

§§ `11(2)(b) What annulment leaves alone`

-- Answers: does annulment leave alone what was done under the instrument before it was annulled, and the maker's power to make further legislation?
-- It does: Article 11(2)(b) says the annulment "does not affect anything done under the subordinate legislation before it is annulled or limit the power of the body empowered to make the legislation to make further legislation".
-- Where the instrument has not been annulled, the paragraph does not apply and the model refuses.
-- src:111 | (b) the annulment does not affect anything done under the subordinate legislation before it is annulled or limit the power of the body empowered to make the legislation to make further legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 11(2)(b) (src:111)
GIVEN `the instrument has been annulled under Article 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11(2)(b): the annulment leaves alone what was done under the instrument and the maker's power to make further legislation` `the instrument has been annulled under Article 11` MEANS
    IF `the instrument has been annulled under Article 11`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 11(2)(b) speaks of an annulment, and the instrument has not been annulled"
